    "evidence_text": " He was born in Kristiania.\n\n He died in Oslo in 1962.\n\n He was a brother of writer and visual artist Anna Lenah Elgstr\u00f6m.\n\nHans \u00d8degaard\n\n He was born in Norderhov.\n\n He studied painting and drawing with Brynjulf Bergslien, Kristian Zahrtmann and Johan Nordhagen.\n\nPoul Simon Christiansen\n\nFolmer Bonn\u00e9n\n\n Kristian Zahrtmann immediately supported the daring work, rewarding Bonn\u00e9n with a stipendium.\n\nFunen Painters\n\n Like Zahrtmann, they abandoned the traditions of the Danish Academy and ventured into Naturalism and Realism.\n\nKristian Zahrtmann\n\nJohannes Wilhjelm\n\n Strongly influenced by Kristian Zahrtmann, he painted bright, colourful landscapes while travelling in Italy.\n\n His works also include religious paintings and portraits.\n\n He frequently visited the artists' colony of Skagen in the north of Denmark where he painted scenes of the dunes and beaches.\n\nPeder Severin Kr\u00f8yer\n\n Kr\u00f8yer was the unofficial leader of the group.\n\nTheodor Philipsen\n\n He also did small figures in wax and clay.",
